Take options into considering asking voters for your ID prior to the election.
Unremovable ink on a person's finger once they cast their vote to prevent someone from voting twice.
Carry out systematic checks on a person's nationality to ensure they are eligible to vote.
A three-year limit on applications for automatic mail-in voting.
Prohibition that political activists process complete mail-in ballots and envelopes of mail-in ballots.
Giving the police the authority to set up lockdowns around election stations.
A change in the law that facilitates intimidation under the Representation of the People Act 1983.
Ban on photography in polling stations.
Requirement that only English may be used in voting stations (excluding Wales).
Intensification of training to ensure employees enforce the rule that voters go to the voting booth alone.
Sir Eric falls over the Metropolitan Police and finds it "amazing" that no criminal charges have been filed after the Tower Hamlets case.
"The Electoral Court has declared Lutfur Rahman and his deputy to be unfit due to litany of corrupt and illegal practices," he said.
He pleaded guilty due to a number of reasons - according to the high requirements in criminal proceedings.
He also criticises the ineffective "check-in checks" of the electoral registration departments of the town halls.
Sir Eric said: "Last-year's court ruling in Tower Hamlets was a warning signal.
