Baden-Württemberg: Police investigate after rocker attack on takeaway
After an attack on an Ulm takeaway, the police are investigating six suspects from the rocker milieu for aggravated land breach.
Evidence and drugs had been secured during apartment searches, the police said on Friday.
Around 20 masked men from a rocker-like group had thrown bottles and stones against the shop window of a takeaway, according to police in July.
After that, they are said to have attacked two guests and slightly injured one.
After that, they fled.
At the snack and the adjacent building there was a damage of 10000 euros.
According to the investigators, it is about a dispute in the Ulm rocker milieu between a Kurdish and a Turkish gang.
Thuringia: Zeiss Meditec closer to sales billion
A high demand for medical technology in Asia has boosted sales of Carl Zeiss Meditec.
In the first nine months of the financial year started in October, Group sales increased by 6.7 percent to 798.6 million euros, as the listed company announced on Friday in Jena.
The Asian business grew disproportionately by 17.1 percent.
According to the interim balance sheet, profit before interest and taxes increased from 89.5 million euros to 110.5 million euros.
The Jena medical technology group intends to exceed the revenue mark of one billion euros this financial year, the Executive Board confirmed.
Zeiss Meditec manufactures devices and equipment for medical practices and clinics.
The company, which belongs to the optics and electronics group Carl Zeiss (Oberkochen), employs almost 3000 people.
